My opinion about peaceful/hostile mines:

Most of the time, you enter the mines relatively early anyway, so a
YASD due to a GWTWOD isn't a major tragedy. I prefer the hostile
mines, because XP is really valuable early on, and you can take down
enemies much easier if you don't have to wait for your pet to do it.
Plus it lowers the risk of losing your pet to a lucky hit by an enemy.
And it means that a bunch of the gnomes and dwarves aren't replaced by
other, nastier things. Usually, my strategy is to take a quick delve
into the mines and grab what I need (a stack of daggers for rouges,
rangers, and wizards (hey, I need something that works once my power
runs out), some good dwarven armor for non-casters (and casters
without a robe), a pickax for everyone) then return to the mazes of
menace until I get reflection or MR and poison resistance, then go
back to the mines and loot them for all they're worth. Most of the
time, it works like a charm.


